        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(anthropic): add claude-haiku-4-5 to claude-cli catalog",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Claude CLI catalog and setup allowlist do not include `claude-haiku-4-5`, so OpenClaw users running the local Claude CLI backend cannot select the full Haiku 4.5 model ref.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis PR adds Haiku 4.5 to:\n\n- the Claude CLI default allowlist and aliases\n- the Claude CLI catalog label, using the existing 200K default context\n- the static plugin manifest with a 200K context window, 64K max output, and 1568px image input\n- the Claude CLI setup/migration expectations so existing configuration flows seed the model\n\nFable is intentionally left to #101453. Mythos is intentionally excluded because current `main` exposes it through the direct Anthropic provider rather than the Claude CLI backend.\n\n## User Impact\n\n`openclaw models list --all --provider claude-cli` can expose `claude-cli/claude-haiku-4-5`. Setup/config migration seeds the ref, and both `haiku-4.5` and `claude-haiku-4-5` normalize to the full model id.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Plugin manifest parses successfully and contains exactly one new Fable/Haiku/Mythos-family Claude CLI row: `claude-haiku-4-5`\n- Verified manifest metadata: 200K context, 64K max output, 1568px image input\n- Node 24 syntax checks passed for the changed TypeScript files\n- Scoped `git diff --check` passed\n- Live Claude CLI agent-turn proof was not obtained because the current subscription session limit was reached\n- GitHub CI is running against head `61dd215e53d50dcefe78b99075ef9764e241b6cf`",
